  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This page brings together several accommodations in the Antibes and Juan-les-Pins area rather than a single address. The Antibes Juan-les-Pins tourist office marks "pets accepted" on about twenty of its hotel listings; conditions and fees change from one establishment to the next.</p>

      <h2>Hotels: pet fee published for 2026</h2>
      <p>Amounts taken from the tourist office's 2026 listings (the unit, per night or per stay, is not specified there):</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hôtel de l'Étoile, 2 avenue Gambetta, Antibes: €5.</li>
        <li>B&amp;B Hôtel Antibes Juan-les-Pins: €6; the listing says pets are welcome "with a fee per night".</li>
        <li>Hôtel Astoria Best Western, 15 avenue Maréchal Joffre, Juan-les-Pins: €8.50.</li>
        <li>La Villa Juan Beach, 5 rue de l'Oratoire, Juan-les-Pins: €10 (hotel open from 9 March to 1 November 2026).</li>
        <li>Hôtel le Collier, 19 boulevard Général Vautrin, Antibes: €20.</li>
        <li>Le 1932 Hôtel &amp; Spa Cap d'Antibes MGallery, 5 avenue Saramartel, Juan-les-Pins: €30.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These listings give no size limit, number of animals, or rule for the restaurant or pool: tell the hotel about your dog when you book.</p>

      <h2>Campsite</h2>
      <p>Camping Les Embruns (63 route de Biot La Brague, Antibes) is ticked "pets accepted" by the tourist office, but its description specifies "pets not allowed in rentals": a dog is therefore possible on a pitch, not in a chalet. Open from 30 March to 30 September 2026.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The tourist office listings show 2026 prices declared by the establishments: confirm the amount and what it covers (per night or per stay) directly with the hotel.</p>
